  Bounded-core conclusion for k=8..11:
    no bounded attackers? True
    consecutive remains exact bounded minimizer? True
    bounded k<12 union floor (consec/min bank) = 1891/5880 = 0.32159864
    THM-530 quoted k>=8 floor from consecutive rows = 1891/5880 = 0.32159864
    The remaining theorem gap is now explicit: prove every span>k+5 row is gentle
    (mu_1/7 >= thr_k), or strengthen the exact bounded bank until a known
    large-spread lemma applies.

============================================================================================
C. Tournament Analysis over proof carriers
============================================================================================
  Pairwise observable: 3*attacker_clearance + 2*witness_support
    + formal_locality - 2*forgetting_penalty.
  score_hist={0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 3: 1, 4: 1, 5: 1, 6: 1}
  directed_3cycles=0
  scc_sizes=[1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1]
  Hamiltonian path=bounded_core_attacker_bank -> continuous_union_floor -> max_D_rhoD_bank -> small_q_survivor_filter -> large_spread_gentle_probe -> raw_single_D_only -> via_max_2over7_shadow
  carrier scores:
    outscore=6 readiness=23  bounded_core_attacker_bank
    outscore=5 readiness=19  continuous_union_floor
    outscore=4 readiness=14  max_D_rhoD_bank
    outscore=3 readiness=12  small_q_survivor_filter
    outscore=2 readiness=10  large_spread_gentle_probe
    outscore=1 readiness=-3  raw_single_D_only
    outscore=0 readiness=-8  via_max_2over7_shadow

============================================================================================
TAKEAWAY
============================================================================================
  max_D rho_D is positive and usually abundant at theta=1/7 on all tested
  hard rows, while theta=2/7 still exposes the known via-max failure.
  For k=8..11, the exact bounded-core bank span<=k+5 contains zero attackers
  and has consecutive shapes as the minimum.  Thus the proof target below
  k=12 is sharply reframed: prove the large-spread rows are gentle, or
  extend the bounded-core bank until an existing spread lemma takes over.
DONE.
